 keel-overlay-wireguard,
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: Keel Core, the appliance every Keel appliance is built on
 The appliance manifest of Keel Core (handbook decisions 0036 and 0041),
 installed as /usr/share/keel/appliances/core.yaml: the five overlays Core
 carries with their state in each installation mode, and Core's own
 processes (sshd, Webmin and postfix) with their ports and checks. A
 systemd drop-in starts monit after those three units, so its first cycle
 does not find them still starting.
 .
 It depends on the five overlay packages, installer, wireguard, etcd,
 crowdsec and vip (0.1.1, the first that ships its units off), and on keel
 0.20.0, the first keel that knows the service VIP (appliance.vip) as well
 as converging the overlays' units and deriving Monit's checks from the
 manifests. Installing it
 enables nothing: keel spec apply sets each overlay to the state the
 instance spec gives it.
